{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Enumeration","symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AStarSearchEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"AStarSearchEvent"}],"role":"symbol","title":"AStarSearchEvent","remoteSource":{"fileName":"AStarSearch.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearch.swift#L18"},"externalID":"s:13ShortestPaths16AStarSearchEventO","modules":[{"name":"ShortestPaths"}]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"What an A* search reports, in order, with the events of the Boost Graph Library’s A* visitor.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"AStarSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Weight"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The source is discovered first, at distance zero, with its estimate: the heuristic’s guess at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its distance to the target (zero for the target itself). Then, while a vertex is open, the one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the smallest distance plus estimate is examined (closed). When that is the target the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"search ends there. Otherwise each of its out-edges is examined in turn with the distance it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"offers its target, the examined vertex’s distance plus the edge’s weight, and is then relaxed,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when the offer is smaller than the target’s distance or the target was not yet discovered, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not relaxed. A relaxed edge to an undiscovered vertex is followed by that vertex’s discovery;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one to a closed vertex, which only an inconsistent heuristic allows, by its reopening (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Boost Graph Library’s black target), after which it is examined again. After its last out-edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the examined vertex is finished. When the target is never reached the search ends once no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex is open.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/astarsearchevent"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","generated":true,"anchor":"Enumeration-Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/discover(_:distance:estimate:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/edgeNotRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/edgeRelaxed(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/examine(_:distance:estimate:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/examineEdge(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/finish(_:distance:)","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/reopen(_:distance:estimate:)"]},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/CustomStringConvertible-Implementations","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/AStarSearchEvent\/Equatable-Implementations"]}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SQ","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"references":{"doc://ShortestPaths/SH":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/SH","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Hashable"},"doc://ShortestPaths/s9EscapableP":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/s9EscapableP","type":"unresolvable","title":"Swift.Escapable"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/AStarSearchEvent/edgeRelaxed(_:distance:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"The edge’s offer beat its target’s distance, which is now ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"distance"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/astarsearchevent\/edgerelaxed(_:distance:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edgeRelaxed"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"distance"},{"kind":"text","text":